1c4e11233","author":{"name":"Akhilesh Arora","email":"akhildawra@gmail.com","date":"2026-04-16T17:46:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"Akhilesh Arora","email":"akhildawra@gmail.com","date":"2026-04-28T15:19:22Z"},"tree":{"sha":"0f6839e70d70213cc32a305d4545580dae5c52fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/trees/0f6839e70d70213cc32a305d4545580dae5c52fd"},"message":"state: preserve nil expiry on user owned registration when no default is configured\n\nWhen a user owned node registers or re registers with a PreAuthKey and the\nclient sends zero client expiry while node.expiry is set to 0, the expiry\ncolumn ends up stored as 0001-01-01 00:00:00 instead of NULL. Two sites in\nHandleNodeFromPreAuthKey build a non nil pointer to regReq.Expiry even when\nthe value is zero time, and the needsDefaultExpiry guard only replaces it\nwhen s.cfg.Node.Expiry > 0, so the pointer to zero time survives to the\ndatabase.\n\nConvert an unset regReq.Expiry to nil before handing it off so the\nneedsDefaultExpiry path is the only place that assigns a non nil pointer.\n\nThis is a narrower sibling of #3170 on the user owned PreAuthKey path. The\nregression was introduced alongside the fix for #3111 in 6337a3db.","parents":[{"sha":"3672a2df3a860bcb97f932d3dc7785406329b49e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/3672a2df3a860bcb97f932d3dc7785406329b49e","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/3672a2df3a860bcb97f932d3dc7785406329b49e"}],"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQIzBAABCgAdFiEE8C93+uC8TaXngX8sVkphQ/EtRnAFAmnwz/oACgkQVkphQ/Et\nRnAyRA//VcGV0HJEeTIX+IdZL56EvIGrkQBaTWQgsczPV6Ve/0XOjTYiFfRIdKs7\nRZZJ9uF3hAJqnyOn7UBPzsPTAReci9ZHVjjXwoPWyUByl7xfcdK2bpn85g5HGdot\nrQekFkd1BRe4j7MPkOKuOpjVY8uA+DqVafnM/wV4GDHY4Prb6wSIOzbDMYxYFEWx\nRYyjUlNu8wUbN5SnQSAIdQNPWv5sJ01osVm2ydnYMVIkhcGVKAgvQ+Wnvl53KuC2\nZpl7hC2KSxnfAKx0VAX0D8Rjj+pmo6+Io3DWi+pY85ynmtgEFOuxnlbyDq7Zm7S1\n9Ck0RDXlSHk1dCIJUGw/fsGMRndzZtPUzovysJHYWmlrU1R/HfsMjmGQsr4J7UW7\nA/mDlOgKsVojtDxylwDAIPbVDqvcVLZmI61AIr8C3VDMDaBl57Pl9JuJka6ILz1j\n+CYOCpMmzO/Q6gmq4DLphRL1MVmGAfkjKqYGbK0yLDc8iHqDqBopSSvpGfa37+gj\n1Uh/04cr1uzJYqa20Gyd5FEYHJzSDgIiJWCiB8Zey5DknEpJuKRj2ZF4aRwc1v+P\nw3gKnVOS8NCJFUfjCn9gQXnW6/lOfV/ZS0SZsbKVdryb8JByvoM3lTtD+z2U9yKW\n46lIMLJWMcBzF3iYpExAMZYhJnqwq9kjuNeU7IDZohcNDhCxUsc=\n=l5hQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","payload":"tree 0f6839e70d70213cc32a305d4545580dae5c52fd\nparent 3672a2df3a860bcb97f932d3dc7785406329b49e\nauthor Akhilesh Arora <akhildawra@gmail.com> 1776361582 +0200\ncommitter Akhilesh Arora <akhildawra@gmail.com> 1777389562 +0200\n\nstate: preserve nil expiry on user owned registration when no default is configured\n\nWhen a user owned node registers or re registers with a PreAuthKey and the\nclient sends zero client expiry while node.expiry is set to 0, the expiry\ncolumn ends up stored as 0001-01-01 00:00:00 instead of NULL. Two sites in\nHandleNodeFromPreAuthKey build a non nil pointer to regReq.Expiry even when\nthe value is zero time, and the needsDefaultExpiry guard only replaces it\nwhen s.cfg.Node.Expiry > 0, so the pointer to zero time survives to the\ndatabase.\n\nConvert an unset regReq.Expiry to nil before handing it off so the\nneedsDefaultExpiry path is the only place that assigns a non nil pointer.\n\nThis is a narrower sibling of #3170 on the user owned PreAuthKey path. The\nregression was introduced alongside the fix for #3111 in 6337a3db.\n","verified_at":"2026-04-28T15:23:01Z"},"event":"committed"},{"sha":"8daaad37c1a5fcbbfef120a27d38056407ccaa39","node_id":"C_kwDOEFLz89oAKDhkYWFhZDM3YzFhNWZjYmJmZWYxMjBhMjdkMzgwNTY0MDdjY2FhMzk","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/8daaad37c1a5fcbbfef120a27d38056407ccaa39","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/8daaad37c1a5fcbbfef120a27d38056407ccaa39","author":{"name":"Akhilesh Arora","email":"akhildawra@gmail.com","date":"2026-04-16T17:46:59Z"},"committer":{"name"